* - geometry_polygon
  - {term}`multipolygon`
  - [1]
  - The geometry representing the spatial extent of the spatial object.

* - inspireIdLocalId
  - {term}`string`254
  - [1]
  - A local identifier, assigned by the data provider.
    The local identifier is unique within the namespace,
    that is, no other spatial object carries the same unique identifier.
    It is the responsibility of the data provider
    to guarantee uniqueness of the local identifier within the namespace.
    
    **WISE**: It is recommended that Data Providers reporting under WFD
    use a localId value identical to the thematicIdIdentifier value.

* - inspireIdNamespace
  - {term}`string`254
  - [1]
  - Namespace uniquely identifying the data source of the spatial object.

    **WISE**:
    For Data Providers in countries not implementing the INSPIRE Directive,
    the country code can be used as placeholder.

* - inspireIdVersionId
  - {term}`string`25
  - [0..1]
  - The identifier of the particular version of the spatial object, 
    with a maximum length of 25 characters. 
    The maximum length has been selected to allow for time stamps based on ISO 8601,
    for example, '2007-02-12T12:12:12+05:30' as the version identifier.

* - thematicIdIdentifier
  - {term}`wiseIdentifier`
  - [1]
  - Unique identifier used to identify the spatial object within the specified identification scheme.

    **WISE**: Unique European identifier of the river basin district.

* - thematicIdIdentifierScheme
  - {term}`IdentifierScheme`
  - [1]
  - Identifier defining the scheme used to assign the identifier.  

    **WISE**: Data Providers reporting under WFD must use the value `'euRBDCode'`. 
    Other Data Providers must use the value `'eionetRBDCode'`.

* - beginLifespanVersion
  - {term}`date`
  - [0..1]
  - Date at which this version of the spatial object 
    was inserted or changed in the spatial data set.  
    The `beginLifespanVersion` value must be provided
    if the `endLifespanVersion` value is provided.

* - endLifespanVersion
  - {term}`date`
  - [0..1]
  - Date at which this version of the spatial object 
    was superseded or retired in the spatial data set.

    **WISE**: The `endLifespanVersion` value is only requested 
    for objects that have been retired (without any replacement).

* - predecessorsIdentifier
  - {term}`wiseIdentifier`
  - [0..n]
  - In a genealogy, the object(s) replaced by the current object.
    {footcite}`INSPIRE_StatisticalUnits_2014`.

    **WISE**: The `predecessorsIdentifier` value is a comma-separated list 
    with the `thematicIdIdentifier` value 
    of the existing object(s) that were replaced.  
    The value must be reported if, and only if, 
    the object replaces one or more objects that were previously reported.  
    Data Providers should report a comma-separated list 
    with the `thematicIdIdentifier` of the object(s) that have been replaced.  
    This attribute does not apply to the case 
    where a newer version of the same object is being reported. 
    In other others, an object never replaces itself.  
    The number of predecessors depends on the `wiseEvolutionType` value.  
    The objects reported as predecessors must exist in the WISE register.

* - predecessorsIdentifierScheme
  - {term}`IdentifierScheme`
  - [0..1]
  - Identifier defining the scheme used to assign the identifier value(s) 
    in the `predecessorsIdentifier` value.

    **WISE**: The value is mandatory if, and only if, one or more predecessors are reported.
    All predecessors must belong to the same identifier scheme.
    The value must be reported if, and only if, the `predecessorsIdentifier` is reported.
    The `predecessorsIdentifierScheme` value is identical to the `thematicIdIdentifierScheme`. 
    In other words, the object being reported can only replace another object 
    in the same identifier scheme.

* - successorsIdentifier
  - {term}`wiseIdentifier`
  - [0..n]
  - In a genealogy, the newly active object(s) that replaces (replace) the current object.
    {footcite}`INSPIRE_StatisticalUnits_2014`

    **WISE**: The `successorsIdentifier` value is a comma-separated list with the
    `thematicIdIdentifier` of the object(s) that replace the current object.
  
    This attribute is **NOT** reported in the 4th cycle spatial datasets. 
    It will be derived by the EEA and populated in the European datasets 
    for the 1st, 2nd, and 3rd cycle of reporting of the WFD River Basin Management Plans,
    for the objects that have being replaced in subsequent reporting cycles.

* - successorsIdentifierScheme 
  - {term}`IdentifierScheme`
  - [0..1]
  - Identifier defining the scheme used to assign the identifier value(s)
    in the `successorsIdentifier` attribute.
    The attribute is mandatory, if and only if one or more successors exist.

* - wiseEvolutionType
  - {term}`WiseEvolutionType`
  - [1]
  - Type of event that produced or modified the version of the object being reported 
    (for example 'noChange', 'creation', 'deletion', 'aggregation').
    {footcite}`INSPIRE_StatisticalUnits_2014`

    **WISE**: 
    The `wiseEvolutionType` value determines the acceptable number of identifiers 
    in the `predecessorsIdentifier` attribute.
    {footcite}`WISE_GISGuidance`
    
* - nameTextInternational
  - {term}`string`254
  - [1]
  - Name, in English. English exonym, or understandable English version 
    of the name of the geographical feature or spatial object. 
    {footcite}`INSPIRE_GeographicalNames_2014`.
  
    **WISE**: For this attribute, the language code is 'eng' (by definition) and is not reported.  
    If an English version does not exist, 
    then provide a transliteration of the national name to the ISO basic Latin alphabet
    (which uses the same 26 letters that comprise the English alphabet).

* - nameText
  - {term}`string`254
  - [1]
  - Name, in the national language. National language endonym,
    or national language version of the name of the geographical feature or spatial object.
    {footcite}`INSPIRE_GeographicalNames_2014`

* - nameLanguage
  - {term}`Language`
  - [1]
  - Language code of the language used in the `nameText` value.
    {footcite}`INSPIRE_GeographicalNames_2014`
    Use the ISO 639-2/B code of the national language used for the object's geographical name.
    {footcite}`iso639-2`

* - designationPeriodBegin
  - {term}`date`
  - [1]
  - Beginning of period defining when 
    the management, restriction or regulation zone 
    was legally designated or became effective in the real world.
    {footcite}`INSPIRE_AreaManagement_2014`

* - designationPeriodEnd
  - {term}`date`
  - [0..1]
  - End of the period defining when
    the management, restriction or regulation zone 
    was legally designated or became effective in the real world.
    {footcite}`INSPIRE_AreaManagement_2014`

    **WISE**: Data Providers are requested to report this information 
    if and only if the object has `wiseEvolutionType = 'deletion'`.

* - zoneType
  - {term}`ZoneType`
  - [1]
  - High-level classification defining the type of Management, Restriction or Regulation Zone.
    {footcite}`INSPIRE_AreaManagement_2014`

    **WISE**: Report `zoneType = 'riverBsinDistrict'`.

* - specialisedZoneType
  - {term}`SpecialisedZoneType`
  - [1]
  - **WISE**: 
    Valid options are 'internationalRiverBasinDistrict' or 'nationalRiverBasinDistrict' 

* - legalBasisName
  - {term}`string`254
  - [0..1]
  - Legislative instrument defining the management, restriction or regulation zone.  

* - legalBasisLink
  - {term}`URL`
  - [0..1]
  - Link to an online authoritative version of the document.

* - legalBasisLevel
  - {term}`LegislationLevelValue`
  - [0..1]
  - The level at which the legislative instrument is adopted.

* - link
  - {term}`URL`
  - [0..1]
